The genealogy of Jesus Christ.
This is the genealogical record of the family lineage of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah was the father of Boaz and Anak. Their mother was Azua. Boaz was the father of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse. Jesse was the father of Eliab, Abinadab, and Shimea.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Azariah was the father of Jotham. Jotham was the father of Ahaz. Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jehoiakim and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to flee to Babylon.
After this, the family line continued. Jeconiah was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Elimelech was the father of Elnathan. Elnathan was the father of Ara. Ara was the father of Rakeen. Rakeen was the father of Shallum. Shallum was the father of Jediael. Jediael was the father of Josabad. Josabad was the father of Zeror. Zeror was the father of Tharkec.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David to the time when the Jewish people had to leave for Babylon. And there were 14 from that time until the Messiah. Jesus Christ was born
Thus the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother Mary and Joseph were pledged to be married. But before they came together, she was found to be with child through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Youssef, was a religious man. He did not want to expose her to the public. Therefore, he planned to divorce her quietly.
But when Joseph was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said to him, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary your wife. For the child who is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
He will bring forth a son. You must give him the name Jesus. For he will save his people from their sins.
All this happened to fulfill what the Lord had said through the prophet:
The virgin will conceive and give birth to a son. She will call him Immanuel. (Isaiah 7:14) The name Immanuel means "God with us."
Joseph woke up. He did what the angel of the Lord had commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
But what happened between them until she gave birth to a son for him. And he named him Yusuf Isa.
