Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This took place when Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, the wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
"Solo, 'where is the child who was born to be king of the Jews? When we were in the East, we saw his star. Now we have come to worship him.'"
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and all the people of Jerusalem were also disturbed.
Now Herod gathered all the chief priests of the people and the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they answered him. "For this is what the prophet has written. 'Behold, a virgin will be with child and will give birth to a son, and they will call him Immanuel,'" which means "God with us."
But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, least of the clans of Judah, from you will come for me the one who will be ruler, and from that time I will seek him until I find him. (Judges 20:18-19)
Subsequently, Herod secretly summoned the wise men who were mad about wisdom. He learned from them precisely the time when the star appeared.
Send them to Bethlehem. He told them, "Go! Search diligently for the child. And when you find him, bring me word. Then I can go and worship him too."
After the wise men of the king had heard him, they departed on their way. The star which they had seen in the East, went before them. And when it came to rest over the place where the child was, they, having seen the glory, were filled with exceedingly great joy.
When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They knelt down and worshipped him. Then, they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. So they returned to their own country by another route. The family of Jesus flees to Egypt.
The wise men departed, Joseph dreamed. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. He said to him, "Rise! Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to look for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. At night, he went to Egypt with his son and his wife Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. Thus the words spoken by the Lord through the prophet were fulfilled. He had said, "I have surely called my son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod realized that the wise men had deceived him. Now he was furiously angry. He gave orders concerning Bethlehem and its region. All the male children who were two years old and under were to be killed. This was in accordance with the time which the wise men had seen the star.
In this way, the words spoken by the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled. He had said,
