After Herod died, Joseph had a dream while he was still in Egypt. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said, "Arise! Take the child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel. Those who were trying to kill the child are dead."
So Joseph got up. He took the child and his mother Mary and they returned to the land of Israel.
But he heard that Archelaus was king of Judea. Archelaus was ruling in place of his father Herod. This made Joseph afraid to go there. He was warned in a dream, and Joseph returned to the land of Galilee instead.
There he lived in a city called Nazareth. So, what the prophets had said about Jesus came true. They said, "He will be called the Nazarene."
