But the things that come out of the mouth come from the heart. These are the things that make you 'unclean'.
Wicked thoughts come from the heart. And these are accompanied by murder, adultery, and other sexual sins. And they are accompanied by theft, false testimony, and lying to others.
Here are the things that make you 'unclean'. However, eating without washing your hands does not make you 'unclean'. "The Faith of the Woman from Canaan"
Jesus left Galilee and went to the region of Tyre and Sidon.
A woman from Canaan who was living near Tyre and Sidon came to him and cried out, "Lord, Son of David! Have mercy on me, please! A demon oppresses my daughter. She suffers greatly."
Jesus didn't say a word. So his disciples came to him. They asked him, "Expel her. She keeps yelling at us."
Jesus answered, "I was sent only to the lost sheep of Israel. They are like a sheep that has wandered off."
And then, the woman fell to her knees before him. "My lord! Help me!" she said.
Answer, "It is not right to take the children's bread and throw it to their dogs."
"Yes, sir," she said. "Even the dogs eat the crumbs that fall from the table of their owners."
And after that, Jesus came and said, "Woman, you have great faith! What you are asking for will be given to you." And immediately her daughter was healed. Jesus feeds the four thousand.
Jesus walked from there. He walked along the Sea of Galilee. Then he went up on a mountain and sat down.
Large crowds came to him. They brought blind people and those who could not walk. They even brought paralytics, those who could not speak, and many other people. They placed them at his feet, and he healed them.
The people were amazed. Those who could not speak were shouting. The disabled were healed. Those who could not walk were walking. Those who were blind could see. Thus the people praised the God of Israel.
From afar, Jesus called his disciples to come to him. He said to them, "I am deeply concerned about these people. They have been with me for three days. They have nothing to eat. I do not want to send them away hungry. If I do that, they will collapse on their way home."
His disciples answered him, "There is no one here to feed them." And they said to him, "How can we feed this vast crowd? Even if we had a whole month to prepare, there wouldn't be enough bread to go around."
How much bread do you have? Jesus asked. "Seven," he replied, "and a few small fish."
Jesus told the group to sit on the ground.
The seven loaves and the fish, and He gave thanks. Then He broke them and gave them to the disciples, and the disciples distributed them to the people.
They all ate and were satisfied. Afterwards, the disciples gathered seven baskets full of leftover pieces.
The number of men who ate was 4,000. Women and children also ate.
After calling the crowd, Jesus entered the boat. He sailed to the region near Magadan.
Jesus is asked for a miraculous sign.
The Pharisees and Sadducees came to test Jesus. They asked him to show them a miraculous sign from heaven.
Answer, "In the evening it goes up into the sky. It says, 'It will be fair. The sky is red.'"
And in the morning she says, "Today will be stormy. The sky is red and cloudy." She understands the meaning of what she sees in the sky. But she cannot understand the signs of what is happening now.
Here is the translation of the provided text: "A wicked and perverse generation seeks for a sign; but no sign will be given to it, except the sign of Jonah." And Jesus went on from them. The leaven of the Pharisees and Sadducees.
The pupils crossed over to the other side of the lake. They forgot to take the bread.
Jesus warned them and said to them, "Beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and the Sadducees."
The pupils discussed this among themselves. They said, "He must be saying this because you didn't bring any bread."
Jesus knew what they were saying. He said, "Your faith is too small! Why are you talking to each other about not having bread?"
Haven't you understood yet? Don't you remember the five breads of five thousand? Don't you remember how many baskets of coins you collected?
Do you not think about the seven loaves of bread for 4000? Do you not think about how many baskets of fragments you have collected?
How is it possible that you do not understand? I was not speaking to you about bread. But beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees.
After the disciples understood that Jesus did not mean for them to observe the leaven used in bread. He was preaching to them from what the Pharisees and Sadducees were saying. Peter says that Jesus is the Christ.
Jesus went into the region of Caesarea Philippi. There he asked his disciples, "Who do people say the Son of Man is?"
They answered, "Some people say John the Baptist; others say Elijah; and others Jeremiah, or one of the prophets."
"What's your opinion on that?" he asked. "Who do you say I am?"
Simon Peter answered, "You are the Christ. You are the Son of the living God."
Jesus answered and said, "Blessed are you, Simon son of Jonah! For flesh and blood has not revealed this to you, but My Father who is in heaven. And I tell you, you are Peter, and on this rock I will build My church; and the gates of Hades shall not prevail against it. I will give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven; and whatever you bind on earth shall be bound in heaven; and whatever you loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven." Then He said to them, "Thus it will be for the birth of the world."
Here is what I say to you. You are Peter. On this rock I will build my church. The gates of hell will not be strong enough to destroy it.
I will give you the keys to the kingdom of heaven. What you bind on earth will be bound in heaven, and what you loose on earth will be loosed in heaven.
Later, Jesus warned his disciples not to tell anyone that he was the Messiah. Jesus speaks about his death which is to come.
From that time on, Jesus began to explain to his disciples what was going to happen to him. He told them, "The Son of Man is going to be betrayed into the hands of men." He continued, "They will kill him, and after three days he will rise again."
Peter pulled Jesus to one side and began to scold him. "My dear, Lord!" he said. "This will never happen to you!"
Jesus turned his face and said to Peter, "Get behind me, Satan! You are an obstacle in my way. You do not have the things of God in mind. On the contrary, you are thinking about the things of people."
Later, Jesus spoke to his disciples. He said to them, "If anyone wants to become my follower, he must deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me."
If he wants to save his life, he will lose it. But if he loses his life for me, he will find it.
What good would it do if someone won the whole world and lost their own soul? Or what could they possibly exchange for their soul?
The Son of Man is coming in the glory of His Father, and His angels will come with Him. And He will reward each person according to what they have done.
What I am going to tell you is true. Some of those standing here will not die before they see the Son of Man coming in his kingdom.
Jesus' appearance was transformed.
After six days, Jesus took Peter, James, and John the brother of James with him. He brought them up onto a high mountain. There they were all alone.
There before them, his form changed. His face shone like the sun. His clothes became white like light.
Suddenly, Moses and Elijah appeared before them. Moses and Elijah were talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus, "Lord, it is good for us to be here. If you wish, I will put up three tents here - one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
And while Peter continued talking, a beautiful cloud enveloped them. A voice from the cloud said, "This is my son, whom I love. I am very pleased with him. Listen to him!"
When the disciples heard this, they were terrified and fell to the ground in worship.
But Jesus came and touched them. He said to them, "Arise," "Do not be afraid."
When they went up, they did not see anyone except Jesus.
They came down from the mountain. On the way down, Jesus said to them what to do. "Do not tell anyone until you see," he said. "Wait until the Son of Man is raised from the dead."
The disciples asked, "Why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?"
Jesus replied, "That's right. It is supposed to be Elijah who comes and renews everything again."
But I tell you, Elijah has already come, and people did not recognize him. They did to him everything they wanted to do. In the same way, they will also make the Son of Man suffer."
After the disciples understood that Jesus was talking to them about John the Baptist, Jesus heals a boy who has a demon.
As they approached the crowd, a man came up to Jesus. He fell on his knees before him.
Sir, he said, have mercy on my child. He is shaking a lot and suffering a lot. He knows how to fall into fire or a lot of water many times.
You brought him to your students. But they couldn't heal him.
O ye wicked and evil generation! Jesus said. How long am I yet with you? How long shall I suffer you? Bring him here to me.
Jesus ordered the demon to come out of the boy, and it came out of him. He was healed at that very moment.
Later, the disciples came to Jesus privately. Alone, they asked him, "Why could we not drive out the demon?"
Your answer is, "Because your faith is too small. What I am about to tell you is true. If your faith was the size of a mustard seed, it would be enough. You could say to this mountain, 'Move from here to there.' And it would move. Nothing would be impossible for you."
