They came together in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man is going to be betrayed into the hands of men."
They will kill him. On the third day, he will rise from the dead. After that, the disciples were filled with deep sorrow. Jesus saves the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter. They asked him, "Doesn't your teacher pay the temple tax?"
Yes, he does, he answered. When Peter entered the house, Jesus began to speak. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "From what sort of people do the kings of the earth collect taxes and duties - from their own children or from others?"
"From others," said Peter. "So the children are not obliged to pay," said Jesus to him.
But we don't want to anger them. So go to the lake and put your fishing line up. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You will find the exact coin you are looking for inside it. Take it and call out to them with it as my and your tax.
